      "id": "LR008",
      "section": "Sequential Logic (Registers)",
      "start_line": 1897,
      "end_line": 1901,
      "text": "Keep work in sequential blocks simple. If a sequential block becomes\nsufficiently complicated, consider splitting the combinational logic into a\nseparate combinational (`always_comb`) block. Ideally, sequential blocks should\ncontain only a register instantiation, with perhaps a load enable or an\nincrement.",
      "sha256": "21c198d95c6a31cf2ed9e901a11384008476b278830e4a0be73c3c5feb192946",
      "characters": 307,
      "use": "General synthesizable language/style guidance, not task requirements or a solution"
    },
    {
      "id": "LR002",
      "section": "Delay Modeling",
      "start_line": 1789,
      "end_line": 1790,
      "text": "Synthesizable design modules must be designed around a zero-delay simulation\nmethodology. All forms of `#delay`, including `#0`, are not permitted.",
      "sha256": "f08d2bb9835cd2c97e28e5887e08b5b4a8a22fbf1363bff522ea521583dc5538",
      "characters": 147,
      "use": "General synthesizable language/style guidance, not task requirements or a solution"
    },
    {
      "id": "LR003",
      "section": "Sequential Logic (Latches)",
      "start_line": 1802,
      "end_line": 1803,
      "text": "If you must use a latch, use `always_latch` over `always`, and use non-blocking\nassignments (`<=`). Never use blocking assignments (`=`).",
      "sha256": "bebab74d9159028626ec42336b8a11d2d3850005988ffd16e22d4d44f7953c7f",
      "characters": 137,
      "use": "General synthesizable language/style guidance, not task requirements or a solution"
